<title>LUXEMBOURG: Court maintains olive oil production levels for 1993/1994.</title>
<headline>Court maintains olive oil production levels for 1993/1994.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Court of Justice rejected on Wednesday an attempt by Italy to annul the European Commission regulation setting olive and olive oil production levels.</p>
<p>Italy challenged the Commission's methods for calculating average yields of olives and olive oil for the 1993/1994 production year.</p>
<p>The court confirmed the Commission's authority to establish and set production levels but noted that member state producers work in concert with the Commisison to determine production levels.</p>
<p>***</p>
<p>EXCERPTS FROM THE JUDGMENT</p>
<p>C-285/94</p>
<p>Republique Italienne</p>
<p>v</p>
<p>Commission des Communautes europeennes,</p>
<p>ayant pour l'objet l'annulation du reglement (CE) no 1840/94 de la Commission, fixant les rendements en olives et en huile pour la compagne 1993/1994 (JO L 193, p. 1)</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>THE COURT rules</p>
<p>1. Le recours est rejete.</p>
<p>2. La Republique italienne est condamnee aux depens.</p>
</text>
